0065: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0066:     """
0067:     Erase each target-color object crossed by the ray pointed by the bar-and-control marker.
0068: 
0069:     Input structure:
0070:     - The background is the dominant color.
0071:     - There is one three-pixel straight marker bar and one singleton control pixel adjacent to the bar center.
0072:     - The remaining non-background color forms multiple 4-connected target objects.
0073: 
0074:     Rule:
0075:     - Cast a straight ray from the marker bar center in the direction away from the adjacent control pixel.
0076:     - Find every 4-connected target-color object that intersects that ray.
0077:     - Recolor all pixels of those hit target objects to the background; all other pixels stay unchanged.
0078: 
0079:     Key insight:
0080:     - The whole object is erased when the center ray touches any of its pixels; the full marker bar width is not swept.
0081:     """
